Maintainer: Huseyin karamelikli <hakperest@gmail.com>
Description: Tests the stability of ordered linear regression models using
    cumulative sums and cumulative sums of squares of recursive residuals.
    For each test, Gaussian Monte Carlo draws on the observed residual grid
    provide a two-sided p-value and matching simultaneous significance bands
    and decisions at the 1, 5, and 10 percent levels. Results include a
    decision table and plotting data. See Brown, Durbin and Evans (1975)
    <doi:10.1111/j.2517-6161.1975.tb01532.x>.
